Lili: Child of Geos is a sweet, family friendly game that reminded me a lot of my gamecube and playstation time.... without the aspect of jumping puzzle.
Pros:
-no jumping puzzles (i mean yeah, it can be a pain for some....I guess?);
-you are looking for flowers;
-You can break vases;
-You can enter people's house and take stuff in their chest;
-You can wear different outfits, hats and have cute (or ugly-cute) pets;
-The story is kinda short, so it's not a game with too much content or a story you really HAVE to focus on;
-Nice soundtrack in the same vibe as Spyro and Jak games;
-LOT of easter eggs. And because you can have a fairy as a pet, wear green,  break vases and ruin people's garden, I'll let you guess which franchise is the most represented in these;
-No ennemies. The foes in this are spirits that you jump on to remove flowers from their back. Since you have no health bar, this is a minigame based on time, and you can buy items to make it easier.
Cons:
-No jumping puzzles, if you wanted this game because it has the style of our childhood video games like spyro, jak or the like....there isn't.
-You are looking for A LOT OF FLOWERS. This game is a punisment if you want the achievement of picking 1000 flowers and 1000 vases because there is 1/3 of vase compared to flowers. I spent 2 hours more on this game ONLY to pick flowers, and I am at 500 vases... If you have no patience for trophies, this game will be your doom.
-You can break a lot of vases, because at one point, if you want money, they are the only source of coins other than a gambling minigame
-The items you find... might have a purpose... well, 5 or so of them do, the rest of the 50 you can ind are here for... I don't know:
-NO ENNEMIES. I mean, when you defeated 3 times (I think?) a foe, it disapears, so no more minigame for you, and if you didn't do a 3 star score, no trophy for you. Also, maybe it's a bug, but for me when I press the rematch button....there is no rematch. The Spirit doesn't even show up on the map before I leave and come back. Or maybe it's just made to be this way? In any case, this button didn't work for me :/
Even with all these cons, this is a very good game to play, if you just want to play a game. For me, this is probably gonna be the game I play again to take a break of the others I have played too much.

